What is Methionine?
Methionine is a protein-based amino acid and lipotropic compound that supports metabolism and fat breakdown processes. It features an α-amino group, an α-carboxylic acid group and an S-methyl thioether side chain. As an essential amino acid, methionine cannot be synthesized by the animal body itself, making dietary supplementation through feed formulations not just beneficial but necessary for modern animal husbandry practices.
